Hello Citizens!

Thank you for trying out and testing the new content that came with the radiation update! This week has been a busy one and, right after releasing v. 0.5.1 of City 20, we got back to work to squash more of the bugs you've been reporting! 

Here's what our latest hotfix tackles: 

[list]
[*] [i]Camera[/i]: fixed a bug where, after loading a game you had saved while inside a building, the game's interior camera would remain active regardless of whether you left the building;
[*] [i]NPCs[/i]: fixed an issue that caused NPCs to get stuck and randomly die when loading a save created with another version of the game;
[*] [i]UI[/i]: fixed a bug where, under certain conditions, players could only select "Donate Item" in the trading screen;
[/list]
As usual, don't forget to join our Discord to get the latest on the development of City 20!

See you on the next one!

Hello Citizens!

Just a few days remain in 2024, and we have a winter holidays gift for you all! City 20's third major roadmap milestone - [b]the Locks and keys Update[/b] - is now available to download!

The December update introduces a new major gameplay mechanic to City 20. People throughout the city will now use keys to protect the most valuable areas of the map, locking places like their homes, factories, stores, and much more! 

But that shouldn't discourage you. If you knock someone out and rifle through their belongings, you might be able to steal the keys! All keys in your possession will appear in your keyring, where you'll also have the chance to locate the door that each key opens. In addition to that, we're also adding a new craftable item, the makeshift lockpick, which can help you get "creative" when it comes to gaining entry to new places.

Whatever your plan is, though, you should act quickly. If citizens realize that their keys have gone missing, they'll report the theft to the faction authorities. Likewise, they will also change their locks - making your efforts effectively useless!

For a quick recap, here's what the update introduces: 
[list]
[*]A brand new Keys and Locks system;
[*]NPCs now react to losing or getting their keys stolen;
[*]Inhabitants will be able to change door locks;
[*]Players can now lockpick doors to gain access to new areas of the map;
[*]A new craftable item, the makeshift lockpick, will help you in your lockpicking endeavors;
[/list]
[b]IMPORTANT SAVES-RELATED INFO:[/b]
Because of the way the update works, this patch WON'T allow you to keep loading your old saves. That said, we want to give everyone the chance to keep playing your old games if you so desire. 

To do so, you will have to access a specific version of the game on Steam, which won't include the December update but will remain compatible with your older saves. Below is a quick step-by-step guide for it. 
[list]
[*]From your Steam library, right click on City 20 and open the "properties" panel;
[*]In the properties window, head to the menu on your left and open the "Betas" tab;
[*]Next, locate the Beta Participation section and click the downward blue arrow to reveal your Beta options;
[*]Locate and select the "0.3.0" Beta Branch, which includes the older version of the game;
[*]Your copy of City 20 will now update. If everything went well, the game should now be labeled as "City 20 [0.3.0] in your library.
[/list]
As usual, feel free to give the new update a go and let us know what you think! If you have any issues with the patch or with accessing the old saves beta, don't hesitate to reach out on the Steam Community Forums or our Discord server!

Enjoy the new update - and happy winter holidays from the whole team at Untold Games!

Hello Citizens!

With the month coming to an end, we just finished working on another major update for City 20! Our next Roadmap Milestone, the NPC update, is now available here on Steam!

As the name suggests, the NPC update contributes to making the inhabitants of City 20 more realistic, with a new set of behaviors and improved survival routines. We also worked on further expanding the game, adding a handful of new content, new items and blueprints - as well as the usual bug-squashing. 

For a full list of what the update introduces, take a look below: 

[i]NPC-Specific Changes[/i]
[list]
[*]Added new behaviors for NPCs in the game. Among other things, hungry NPCs might now ask the player for help, while others might decide to attack and rob you;
[*]Improved survival routines for NPC, which should help them tackle the challenges of post-nuclear life;
[*]Added a new NPC List - accessible through the player menu - which will contain general info about known NPCs;
[/list]
[i]General Gameplay Changes[/i]
[list]
[*]Introduced new items and blueprints for players to discover;
[*]Deer, foxes, and wolves will now interact with placed traps;
[*]Improved visuals for some of the in-game items and assets;

[/list]
[i]Bug Fixes and Improvements[/i]
[list]
[*]Improved graphics performances across the game;
[*]Solved several bugs reported by the community over the past few weeks;
[*]Improved visuals and animations for some of the in-game characters;
[*]General performance improvements;
[/list]
[i]Known Issues[/i]
[list]
[*]Interior lighting bug: when loading saves created before this update, interior lighting might not trigger properly in certain areas;
[/list]

As usual, don't forget to let us know what you think of the update below or hop into our Discord to get the latest news on the development of City 20!

[h2]Steam Autumn Sales[/h2]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44883359/2109d536687577f9d690b1afa4b8d668c35a2350.png[/img]
To celebrate the update, City 20 has also joined the Steam Autumn Sales! From November 27th to December 4th, the game will be 20% off across all regions! 

Don't miss the opportunity to join us and explore the city!

Hello Citizens!

On the spookiest day of the year, we have some great news to share! The [i][b]October Update[/b][/i] - the first milestone on our road to 1.0 - is finally available! 

Here is a list of the main changes this patch introduces: 

[b]Gameplay and Features[/b]
[list]
[*]Added a "locate NPC" option which allows you, once an activity is unlocked, to discover the location of any NPCs involved it;
[*]Added a brand new map hotkey! You can now access the map by hitting M on your keyboard or by holding the Options button if you are using a gamepad;
[*]Increased the maximum number of waypoints you can mark on your map from 2 to 6;
[*]Wolves will now also behave aggressively during the day - stay clear of the forests!
[*]The Bartender and Radio Speaker NPCs will now work in turns, with different NPCs covering the morning and evening shifts. This increases the total amount of time their respective doors stay open and gives you longer to interact with them; *
[*]Improved NPC survival routines throughout the game; *
[/list]

[b]Improvements and Fixes[/b]
[list]
[*]Reworked and improved some elements of the in-game UI;
[*]Rebalanced food fullness values - which will influence how much food you need to survive;
[*]Improved some of the in-game option menus;
[*]Fixed a handful of technical and loading-related issues;
[/list]

[b]Known issues[/b]
[list]
[*]There's a chance that Goga might not kick players out after three days - effectively allowing you to use his property indefinitely;
[*]When loading an older save, some blueprints might be displayed in different crafting modes - which temporarily gives you multiple ways to craft certain items;
[*]When loading an older save, the Bartender and Radio Speaker might be working shorter hours than expected;
[/list]

[b]NOTE[/b]: changelog entries marked with a * require you to start a new game to take effect. As with any major update, we suggest starting a new game to avoid any unexpected issues!

Enjoy the update and happy Halloween! As usual, don't forget to join our Discord to get the latest news on the development of City 20!

Hello Citizens, 

We have a new Hotfix for City 20 - fresh off the furnace!  

As some of you reported a couple of potentially game-breaking bugs over the past week, we diverted some of our team to ensure those could be tackled and squashed as soon as possible!

Below is a full list of the issues this patch addresses:

[i]Crash Fixes[/i]
[list]
[*] Fixed several issues that would cause the game to crash or get stuck on a black screen when loading a save;
[*] Solved a problem with the game crashing when radio messages unlocked new in-game events; 
[*] Fixed a crash that would happen when the Let's Drink Together activity wasn't completed;
[*] General improvements of performance and resources management;
[/list]

Our first major update is also due soon, with more fixes and improvements on the way! As usual, don’t forget to join our Discord to chat with the dev team and follow the development of our project!

Hello Citizens, 

New month, new set of fixes from our team! 

Hotfix 2 just landed, tackling a few more of the issues you reported over the past week! In addition, we’re also introducing a couple of [b]quality-of-life improvements[/b] that should make your gameplay a bit easier and pave the way for future content!

Here’s the full list of changes for this patch:

[i]Crash Fixes[/i]
[list]
[*] Fixed an issue where dead NPCs would continue to play their animations, crashing the game in the process;
[*] Fixed a problem where listening to a radio message about the Market would crash the game; 
[*] Solved a problem with live prey that would crash the game when emptying traps;
[*] Fixed a crash that would happen when emptying fuel tanks in a menu with two containers;
[/list]

[i]Exploits and Softlocks[/i]
[list]
[*] Changed the way ingredients are handled during crafting - which now allows you to remove blueprints when ingredients don’t match and restart production;
[*] Fixed an exploit which allowed players to duplicate items in their inventory;
[*] Solved an issue with guard shifts which would softlock the game when trying to pay the Mozga entry fee;
[/list]  

[i]Misc Changes[/i]
[list]
[*] Increased the time NPCs will wait before they try to kick you out while trespassing;
[*] NPCs wishes now take a bit longer to change, giving you more time to find the relevant items;
[*] Replaced placeholder text throughout the game;
[/list]

In the next few days, we’ll also be sharing our initial roadmap for the future of City 20! As usual, don’t forget to join our Discord to chat with the dev team and follow the development of our project!

Hello citizens of City 20! Our first hotfix is out! 

This patch focuses on addressing the following issues with the game:

[list]
[*]Fixed a bug where the game would crash if players added an ingredient to an existing construction yard after loading a save;
[*] Fixed an issue where the death and funeral of a guard NPC would crash the game if said guard had already buried a corpse in the past (seriously, don't ask);
[*] Fixed an issue where loading a save with dead NPCs on the map would crash the game;
[/list]

Thank you again for your support and help as we continue working on City 20! Don't forget to join our Discord to keep up with City 20's journey!
